-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party work OpenBot builds on
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mbotmake (charely6/mbotmake), GPL-3.0
  The .makerbot meta.json template (openbot/slicing/data/meta_template.json) and parts
  of the G-code conversion approach are derived from it.

queue3d (garfield-arlene/queue3d), MIT License
  The Replicator+ OrcaSlicer profile (openbot/slicing/data/replicator_plus_base.json)
  was adapted from its profile; its hardware notes informed the network protocol work.

OrcaSlicer (SoftFever/OrcaSlicer), AGPL-3.0
  Bundled unmodified in the macOS app as a separate program and run as a subprocess.
  Its printer profiles (Creality) are read at runtime. Source:
  https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer

Protocol research also drew on tjhorner/makerbot-rpc, tjhorner/node-makerbot-rpc,
abdyfranco/makerbot-php and charely6/makerbot-gen5-api (reference only, no code copied).

Python libraries used at runtime, under their own licenses: PySide6/Qt (LGPL-3.0),
qasync (BSD-2-Clause), cryptography (Apache-2.0/BSD), aiohttp (Apache-2.0),
zeroconf (LGPL-2.1), keyring (MIT), pyserial (BSD-3-Clause).

